---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy | Lakeland Repair";
const pageDescription = "Privacy policy, data collection disclosures, TCPA communications consent, and data protection standards for Lakeland Repair.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  
  <!-- Custom Legal Hero -->
  <section class="relative bg-brand-teal text-white overflow-hidden py-16 lg:py-24 border-b border-teal-800">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,_var(--tw-gradient-stops))] from-teal-700/40 via-brand-teal-dark to-brand-teal-dark z-0"></div>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-teal-800/80 border border-teal-600/50 text-teal-100 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase mb-6">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-amber" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
        <span>Legal Documentation</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-teal-100/80 text-sm">Last Updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-brand-surface">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl shadow-xl border border-gray-100 p-8 sm:p-12 lg:p-16">
        
        <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 marker:text-brand-teal">
          
          <div class="bg-brand-teal/5 border-l-4 border-brand-teal p-6 rounded-r-2xl mb-12">
            <p class="m-0 font-medium text-brand-teal-dark">
              Lakeland Repair ("we", "us", or "our") operates a consumer connection, referral, and dispatch matching service connecting consumers in Lakeland and Polk County, Florida with independent third-party appliance repair contractors. This Privacy Policy details the types of information we collect, how that information is utilized and shared with independent service providers, and your privacy rights.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">1. Scope and Service Description</h2>
          <p>
            This website acts as an independent marketing and referral service that connects consumers seeking appliance repair services with local, independent technicians and service companies. By accessing this website, placing a phone call to the telephone numbers displayed on our website, or submitting your contact details, you acknowledge and agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">2. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>We may collect several categories of information from and about users of our service:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Personal Contact Information:</strong> Full name, telephone number, email address, physical service address, ZIP code, and unit/apartment numbers provided when requesting appliance diagnostics or repair dispatch.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Request Details:</strong> Appliance brand, model, symptoms, appliance location, and preferred service scheduling windows.</li>
            <li><strong>Call Logs & Audio Recordings:</strong> Inbound and outbound phone calls made to our published telephone numbers may be monitored or recorded for quality assurance, compliance, verification, technician dispatch accuracy, and training purposes. Telephony data such as caller ID, call duration, timestamp, and routing information is collected automatically.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical & Browsing Data:</strong> Internet Protocol (IP) address, browser type and version, operating system, referring URL, pages viewed, time spent on pages, and device identifiers collected through standard server logs, cookies, and web analytics tools.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">3. How We Use and Share Your Information</h2>
          <p>We use the information collected for specific business and operational purposes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Connecting You with Independent Service Providers:</strong> We share your service request details, name, phone number, and address with independent third-party appliance repair contractors and dispatch networks operating in your geographic area to fulfill your service request, provide estimates, and perform repair services.</li>
            <li><strong>Customer Service & Dispatch Management:</strong> Facilitating appointments, technician ETA updates, diagnostic coordination, and service inquiries.</li>
            <li><strong>Quality Assurance & Compliance:</strong> Reviewing call recordings and service interactions to maintain service standards, prevent fraud, and verify customer consent.</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics & Improvement:</strong> Analyzing website traffic patterns and advertising campaign performance to enhance user experience.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal contact information to unrelated third-party marketing lists or spam brokers. Information is shared strictly for the purpose of fulfilling your appliance repair inquiry or as required by law.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">4. TCPA Consent & Automated Communications Disclosure</h2>
          <p>
            By dialing any telephone number published on this website, or by submitting your contact information through our platform, you provide your express written consent under the Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA) and applicable state laws to be contacted by Lakeland Repair, its dispatch partners, and its network of independent local service contractors.
          </p>
          <p>
            You agree that communications may include live telephone calls, automated telephone dialing systems (ATDS), artificial or prerecorded voice messages, and SMS/MMS text messages to the telephone number you provided regarding your service inquiry, appointment scheduling, and technician arrival times.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Voluntary Consent:</strong> Consent to receive automated or marketing communications is not a condition of purchasing any goods or services.</li>
            <li><strong>Message & Data Rates:</strong> Standard message and data rates applied by your mobile service carrier may apply to text communications.</li>
            <li><strong>Opt-Out Instructions:</strong> You may opt out of text messaging at any time by replying "STOP" to any SMS message received. To opt out of telephone calls, you may notify our dispatch desk during a call or submit a request via our contact desk.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">5. Call Recording & Quality Monitoring</h2>
          <p>
            Please be advised that all telephone calls placed to or received from our dispatch numbers may be recorded and monitored for quality assurance, employee and contractor training, dispute resolution, and regulatory compliance. If you do not wish for your call to be recorded, please inform the representative immediately at the beginning of the call.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">6. Cookies, Tracking & Web Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We utilize cookies, web beacons, and standard analytics scripts (such as Google Analytics and call attribution software) to track site interactions, measure marketing efficacy, and remember user preferences. You can configure your browser to reject cookies or notify you when cookies are being set; however, certain site features may have reduced functionality if cookies are disabled.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">7. Third-Party Service Providers & Contractors</h2>
          <p>
            Independent service contractors and technicians who receive your inquiry operate as independent businesses with their own privacy practices and terms. Once you are connected with or hire an independent technician, their handling of your information during the in-person repair visit is governed by their respective business practices.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">8. Data Security & Storage</h2>
          <p>
            We maintain commercially reasonable technical, physical, and administrative safeguards designed to protect personal information against unauthorized access, destruction, loss, or alteration. While we implement standard security protocols, no data transmission over the Internet or cellular network is guaranteed to be 100% secure.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">9. State Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA, Florida Digital Bill of Rights)</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on your state of residence, you may have specific statutory rights concerning your personal information, including the right to know what personal data is collected, request deletion of your information, and opt out of the disclosure or sharing of personal data. To submit a verifiable consumer privacy request, please contact us using the details below.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our services and website are strictly directed to adult homeowners and property managers aged 18 and older. We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under 13 years of age.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to amend this Privacy Policy at any time. Any revisions will be reflected on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date. Continued use of our website or calling services constitutes acceptance of the modified policy.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">12. Contact Information</h2>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 mt-6">
            <p class="m-0 text-sm">
              If you have any questions, comments, or data privacy requests, please contact our administrative desk:<br><br>
              <strong>Lakeland Repair Compliance & Privacy Desk</strong><br>
              120 E Pine St, Suite 4<br>
              Lakeland, FL 33801<br>
              Phone: <a href="tel:+18632780714" class="text-brand-amber font-bold hover:underline">(863) 278-0714</a>
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
